WEBVTT

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:08.500
Welcome to our final lesson, creators!

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:12.433
Here are our three files, all finished.

00:00:12.433 --> 00:00:14.167
Before we share our game,

00:00:14.167 --> 00:00:18.167
we have one more important job: testing.

00:00:18.333 --> 00:00:22.800
Developers save and test their work often. Save...

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:24.800
and Run.

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:30.267
Let's play our game like a tester, and check every part.

00:00:30.633 --> 00:00:37.700
First, we select two cards. Do they flip? Yes!

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:41.200
Now let's find a matching pair.

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:46.600
They turn green, and stay face up. Perfect.

00:00:47.167 --> 00:00:50.133
Now two cards that don't match.

00:00:50.133 --> 00:00:55.900
They show for a moment, then turn back over. Correct!

00:00:56.267 --> 00:01:03.967
Is the moves counter right? Three turns, three moves. Yes!

00:01:04.333 --> 00:01:08.167
Is the timer counting? Yes.

00:01:08.167 --> 00:01:11.600
It started with our very first click.

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:13.767
Let's finish the game...

00:01:13.767 --> 00:01:16.833
and there's the celebration screen.

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:20.367
Play again starts a fresh game.

00:01:20.367 --> 00:01:22.033
And if we change the difficulty

00:01:22.033 --> 00:01:25.433
to Easy, we get four pairs.

00:01:25.833 --> 00:01:28.033
Everything works!

00:01:28.033 --> 00:01:32.533
Testing helps us find mistakes before other people do.

00:01:33.533 --> 00:01:36.700
But what happens when something goes wrong?

00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:39.933
Let's look at a practice project.

00:01:40.333 --> 00:01:42.767
In this practice project,

00:01:42.767 --> 00:01:47.267
someone typed styles.css, with an extra s.

00:01:47.633 --> 00:01:50.600
We click Run... and oh no!

00:01:50.600 --> 00:01:54.433
All our colours and cards have disappeared.

00:01:54.833 --> 00:01:59.933
Let's investigate. The HTML looks fine.

00:01:59.933 --> 00:02:02.600
The CSS looks fine.

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:06.800
So, the problem must be the link between them.

00:02:07.167 --> 00:02:09.967
The file is called style.css,

00:02:09.967 --> 00:02:12.767
but the link says styles.css.

00:02:12.767 --> 00:02:17.500
The browser can't find a file with that name!

00:02:17.867 --> 00:02:22.933
Let's remove the extra s, save, and run again.

00:02:23.733 --> 00:02:25.433
Fixed!

00:02:25.433 --> 00:02:29.533
Finding and fixing mistakes like this is called debugging.

00:02:29.533 --> 00:02:33.667
Every developer does it, every single day.

00:02:34.667 --> 00:02:38.067
Now it's your turn to make this game your own.

00:02:38.067 --> 00:02:40.833
Here are some challenges.

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:46.033
Challenge one: change the background colour of the page.

00:02:46.433 --> 00:02:50.867
Challenge two: change the heading to something new.

00:02:51.233 --> 00:02:53.967
Challenge three: try different

00:02:53.967 --> 00:02:58.000
Quicksand font weights, from 300 to 700.

00:02:58.367 --> 00:03:00.467
Challenge four: change the number

00:03:00.467 --> 00:03:03.100
of pairs in one of the levels.

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:05.800
You can go up to eight.

00:03:06.167 --> 00:03:10.900
Challenge five: make the cards bigger or smaller.

00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:15.733
Challenge six: give the card backs a new colour.

00:03:16.133 --> 00:03:17.700
And challenge seven:

00:03:17.700 --> 00:03:20.833
create your very own version of the game.

00:03:20.833 --> 00:03:25.933
Maybe with letters, colours, or shapes instead of numbers?

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:29.167
Don't worry about breaking things.

00:03:29.167 --> 00:03:34.033
You can always fix them. That's how we learn!

00:03:47.233 --> 00:03:51.333
Take a moment, and look at what you have achieved.

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:55.767
You started with an empty HTML document.

00:03:55.967 --> 00:03:58.467
You learned how to structure a webpage,

00:03:58.467 --> 00:04:03.867
style it with CSS, and bring it to life using JavaScript.

00:04:04.067 --> 00:04:06.167
And now, you have built your very

00:04:06.167 --> 00:04:09.067
own memory matching game!

00:04:09.633 --> 00:04:12.333
Remember, every great developer started by

00:04:12.333 --> 00:04:15.700
learning one small thing at a time.

00:04:15.867 --> 00:04:20.000
Keep experimenting. Keep creating.

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:23.300
And never stop being curious.

00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:27.000
This is Paisley Studio.

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:32.867
Imagine it. Build it. Make it yours.
